# Named Tables and Arrays

A markdown table preceded by a `table:` directive becomes a data source.
Columns are arrays; calc blocks combine them element-wise and aggregate them.

<!-- table: rates (role, rate, hc) -->
| Role   | Hourly rate | Headcount |
|--------|-------------|-----------|
| Senior | $250        | 2         |
| Junior | $150        | 5         |

## Element-wise arithmetic

line_costs = rates.rate * rates.hc
# Expected: [$500.00, $750.00]

uplifted = rates.rate * 1.1
# Expected: [$275.00, $165.00]

## Aggregates

total = sum(line_costs)
# Expected: $1250.00

average_rate = avg(rates.rate)
# Expected: $200.00

cheapest = min(rates.rate)
# Expected: $150.00

largest_team = max(rates.hc)
# Expected: 5

roles = count(rates.role)
# Expected: 2

people = sum(rates.hc)
# Expected: 7

## Per-row display

| Role   | Line cost      |
|--------|----------------|
| Senior | {{line_costs}} |
| Junior | {{line_costs}} |

Grand total: {{total}} across {{people}} people.
